id: numerics/exponentiate/0349
area: numerics
op: BigInt::exponentiate
in: bigint:1 bigint:18446744073709551616
out: value: bigint:1
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: BigInt exponentiation converts the exponent to a 32-bit integer, so an exponent of 2^31 or more raises a .NET OverflowException that escapes the engine, where 1n, -1n and 0n have their exact powers and any other base is a RangeError at the representation's limit. Answered by Broiler.JS docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, SJL-4.5 (the BigInt kernel; the correction of Power's 32-bit exponent).
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-numeric-types-bigint-exponentiate ref:numericsref@1
script: 1n ** 0x10000000000000000n
since: 6

